            <ArticleTitle>Complications of day-case angiography using 5F catheters.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>102-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Questionnaires were sent retrospectively to patients who had undergone day-case angiography at a British teaching hospital to evaluate the complications suffered after leaving hospital. In 1992, 5F catheters were used in 61 day-case patients. On analysis of the responses and detailed follow-up in areas of concern, no unexpected complication was found. It is concluded that day-case angiography using 5F catheters is associated with low morbidity after discharge home.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
